# Routing

## Paths
- Every path is a constant in lib/config/routes/route_paths.dart: /, /onboarding, /auth/phone, /auth/otp, /auth/name, /auth/dob, /welcome, /home, /explore, /rewards, /orders, /settings and /product/:id. Use the helper methods to build paths with parameters.
- Never write a path string literal outside route_paths.dart.

## Guard
- SessionBloc owns the session: unknown, unauthenticated, registering, authenticated.
- resolveAuthRedirect in auth_redirect.dart is a pure function of the session and the location. It is unit-tested for every status and location combination.
- unknown: hold on the launch route (bootstrap restores the session before the first frame, so this is never visible).
- unauthenticated: only onboarding, /auth/phone and /auth/otp; everything else goes to /onboarding.
- registering: onboarding, all auth routes and /welcome; everything else goes to /auth/name.
- authenticated: launch, onboarding and auth routes go to /welcome right after registration and to /home otherwise.
- RouterRefreshStream adapts the SessionBloc stream into the refresh listenable.

## Structure
- The five-tab shell is a StatefulShellRoute.indexedStack. Inactive branches are wrapped in TickerMode so their animations stop.
- /product/:id is a top-level route above the shell. An unknown id renders the not-found state inside the route.
- Registration name and date of birth share one RegistrationBloc provided by a ShellRoute so entered data survives back navigation.
- Route builders resolve Blocs from get_it and provide them with BlocProvider. Screens never resolve dependencies themselves.

## Transitions
- Build every page through route_transitions.dart. Durations and curves come from MotionTokens and are scaled by the MotionProfile.
- Auth steps use the shared-axis horizontal transition, tab switches use fade-through, product detail uses a fade-scale transition that keeps Hero animations working.
- With the minimal motion tier transitions collapse to a short fade.
